# Per-package coverage floors (ratchet: only raise, never lower).
# Baseline measured on the CI toolchain pinned in .github/workflows/ci.yaml
# (Go 1.26.6) with `go test -coverprofile=coverage.out ./...` + coverage-gate.sh:
#   approval 76.98  checks 71.75  delivery 67.16  evidence 62.59
#   pipeline 74.23  safeio 72.67
# Baseline for the packages added by issues #103/#119 was measured on Go 1.27.1:
#   cmd/ai-team 60.85  artifactstore 77.53  worker 96.80
#
# Floors sit below the measured baseline so the gate stays stable across Go
# patch/toolchain differences (instrumented statement counts differ between Go
# releases — Go 1.27 measures pipeline at 75.9 against a 74.23 baseline on
# 1.26.6). The margin is NOT uniform: it is whatever the package needs.
# Packages measured on the pinned CI toolchain keep a tight margin
# (delivery 0.4pp, pipeline 0.4pp, evidence 0.7pp, approval 1.3pp); packages
# whose floor was set from a coarser or older measurement keep a wider one
# (checks ~7pp, safeio ~12pp), and the three added on Go 1.27.1 keep ~1.5-2pp
# because the CI toolchain differs from the machine they were measured on.
# Raising a floor after an improvement is expected; lowering one is rejected
# by review.
PKG_APPROVAL_FLOOR=75.7
PKG_ARTIFACTSTORE_FLOOR=76.0
PKG_CHECKS_FLOOR=64.6
PKG_CMD_AI_TEAM_FLOOR=59.0
PKG_DELIVERY_FLOOR=66.8
PKG_EVIDENCE_FLOOR=61.9
PKG_PIPELINE_FLOOR=73.8
PKG_SAFEIO_FLOOR=60.0
PKG_WORKER_FLOOR=95.0
